Rules of Exception Law

1. Logic Puzzle, "For every exception there is an exception, except the exception.".

2. How exception theory came to be, "It started with 'For every exception there is and exception.'. Which then logically led to 'except the exception'. Then came a question; how many of those "except the exception"'s 'exception' are there? It was a hard thing to figure out and crack. Then, Exception Theory became what you see. It was all derived from that.

3. P is for Point, it is the substrate. A Point is infinite. An unbound point is infinite. P is bound to D. The ultimate Point is the total set of infinities, Absolute Infinity.

4. D is for Descriptor, a descriptor describes a point. A Descriptor is Finite. There are finite ways to describe a Point. An unbound Descriptor would be infinite. D is bound to P. Because an unbound descriptor is infinite, this allows for it to be across infinite Points, even though when bound to P, D becomes Finite. The ultimate Descriptor is the total set of finite, Absolute Finite.

5. T is for Traverser, it traverses. A Traverser is Indeterminate. A Traverser can traverse any number of (P°D) as it is indeterminate. There is no limit to the number of T bound at a (P°D) because it is indeterminate. Examples are consciousness, entanglement, and gravity. T binds to D. T is limited by the descriptors it binds to, not all T bind to all D due to indeterminacy. T does not bind to P. T binds anywhere in (P°D) as they are bound. T travels P by using D as (P°D) are bound. The ultimate Traverser is the total set of indeterminate, Absolute Indeterminate.

6. The binding and interaction are the same. Binding/Interaction is inherent and intrinsic. There is only an illusion that Binding/Interaction is weaker or stronger. T does not collapse into a singularity with (P°D) because it is indeterminate.

7. The Binding/Interaction of PD or PDT is what makes something Substantiated (Moment/Exception) or Unsubstantiated (Potential). Pure (P°D) is Unsubstantiated. (P°D) with T is Substantiated.

8. 'Something' and its parts, everything and anything, is relational. There is only pure relativism.

9. E is for 'Something'. 'Something' is everything and anything. 'Something' is comprised of PDT. PDT generates 'Something'. Outside of 'Something' is still 'Something'.

10. E = (P°D°T)

11. (P°D)°T or T°(P°D) as the T placement does not matter due to (P°D) Binding/Interaction. There can never be (D°P) as a Descriptor must describe a Point.

12. "True" Absolute Nothing cannot exist. The moment it can have a name or be described means it can be described and thus it is 'Something'. One can only attach 'Something' to it, this leads to there always being 'Something'.






























